title: Authorizations › New Case › Review & submit › After sending
route: /authorizations/case/R-1701, then /dashboard, /authorizations and /manager
intro: What changes once the request is signed and sent: the new case opens, the Dashboard shows it as Received, the Authorizations queue lists it, Case Manager stops listing it under Being prepared, and the patient's record gains the request. An existing patient is never copied: the request joins the patient, the treatment episode and the authorization it belongs to. The draft's own address turns into a 'was sent' page.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "The request is signed and sent"
screen sCase "The new case opens\nCase page for R-1701 with its tabs\nHistory has the lines written at signing"
goto gCase "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Header and buttons"

group gDash "Dashboard"
  screen sDash "Dashboard\nThe request is in the table and in its drawer: '/dashboard?request=R-1701'\nChip 'Received', held by Navigator"
  process pCount "In the lifecycle counts 'Received' goes up by one\nThe 'Preparing' count goes down by one: a saved draft was counted there until now"
  toast tToast "Toast: 'Sent to the payer'\nBell notification: 'Sent to the payer'"
endgroup
goto gOpen "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Open and read a request"

group gQueue "Authorizations queue"
  screen sQ "Queue\nA row for the request: patient, payer, level of care, type\n'Payer has it. Navigator checks again in 30 minutes'"
  process pQ "It sits in the band of the payer's usual decision time\nOnly a viewer who can see the case's site sees the row"
endgroup
goto gQueue "Continues in: Authorizations › Queue › Read and open a request row"

group gPat "The patient's record"
  store stLink "The request is linked to its patient, treatment episode, authorization and verification\nA new patient becomes a patient\nA review, renewal or modification joins its authorization: History gets 'Continued stay request signed and sent'\nA new stay for a known patient gets its own episode and a pending authorization"
  process pBook "The next search finds the patient once, with the new authorization shown as Not approved yet\nA second new case for them finds this one as a possible duplicate"
  process pVer "The check from step 2 is the same record Eligibility & Benefits shows\nIt is filed under the case id"
endgroup
goto gEb "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › List › What the screen shows"

group gWas "The draft's own address"
  click cBr "Press the browser's Back button, or reopen the case's address"
  screen sWas "R-1701 was sent\n'It was signed and sent to the payer (demo). The agents are following it from the Dashboard.'\nIf the store does not hold the request: 'R-1701 is with the payer'"
  process pNoSign "'This case is no longer being prepared'\n'Nothing more is needed here.'\nIt cannot be signed a second time"
  click cOpenCase "Click 'Open the case'"
  click cOpenDash "Click 'Open it on the Dashboard'"
  click cBackCM "Click 'Back to Case Manager'"
endgroup

group gCM "Case Manager › Active cases"
  screen sCM "Case Manager\n'N active cases.' and 'N are still being prepared.'"
  process pGone "The case leaves the 'Being prepared' card\nThe 'still being prepared' count goes down by one"
  process pBadge "The sidebar badge on 'Case Manager' no longer counts it"
  click cSent "Click the 'N sent today' button"
  process pSentN "The count is one higher (4 becomes 5)"
  process pLedger "The tracker of active cases gains a row for the request"
endgroup
goto gDash2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Requests table › Order, rows and paging"
goto gCM2 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › A new case joins the tracker"

s1 --> sCase --> gCase
s1 --> sDash --> pCount
sDash --> tToast
sDash --> gOpen
s1 --> sQ --> pQ --> gQueue
s1 --> stLink --> pBook
stLink --> pVer --> gEb
s1 --> cBr --> sWas --> pNoSign
pNoSign --> cOpenCase --> sCase
pNoSign --> cOpenDash --> sDash
pNoSign --> cBackCM --> sCM
s1 --> sCM --> pGone --> pBadge
sCM --> cSent --> pSentN --> gDash2
sCM --> pLedger
pLedger -.-> gCM2
